course: dictionary
lesson: 14261
title: Nevertheless: even so
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words link two ideas and show how they fit together. Nevertheless is one of them. It tells you that something happened in spite of what was just said. «It was raining; nevertheless, we went out.» The rain was a reason to stay in, but we went out anyway.
explain: Look at the words before it. The first part gives a problem or a reason against something, and nevertheless shows that the next part happens anyway. «The test was hard. Nevertheless, Maya kept trying.» Hard is the problem, and kept trying is what she did in spite of it.
explain: In speech you would say «but», «still» or «even so». In formal writing, such as essays and exams, nevertheless is the stronger choice. When it starts a sentence, put a comma after it: «Nevertheless, the team played on.»
fact: Nevertheless means in spite of what has just been said; even so.
fact: «Nevertheless» means however, all the same, in formal writing.
fact: Nevertheless shows a contrast: the second idea goes against what you would expect from the first.
fact: Phrases you may see are «but nevertheless» and «nevertheless, it is true that...».
exercise: «The bike had a flat tyre; nevertheless, Ali rode it to school.» What does nevertheless show? | *Ali rode to school even though the tyre was flat | The tyre was never flat at all | Ali stayed at home because of the flat tyre | Ali fixed the tyre and bought a new bike
exercise: «It was cold. Nevertheless, we swam in the lake.» Which word could replace nevertheless here? | *Even so | Before | Because | Instead
exercise: «Lena had a bad cold. Nevertheless, she sang in the concert.» Why does the author use nevertheless? | *To show she sang although she had a cold | To show she had a cold because of the concert | To show she did not sing | To show it was her birthday
test: «Dad was tired after work; nevertheless, he cooked dinner for us.» What does nevertheless show? | *Dad cooked dinner even though he was tired | Dad cooked dinner because he was tired | Dad cooked dinner for his friend | Dad was too tired to cook
test: Which word means nearly the same as nevertheless in formal writing? | Quickly | Afterwards | Because | *All the same
exam: «The sea was rough and cold; nevertheless, the swimmers dived in.» Which best describes what nevertheless tells us? | The swimmers were scared of the sea | *The swimmers dived in even though the sea was rough and cold | The swimmers came out at once | The sea was calm and warm
